WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:11.500
Let’s start with a question and, please,
don’t cheat and look it up on Google…

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.429
How many immigrants have been deported by
Donald Trump?

00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:15.429
Think about it!

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:18.750
During the electoral campaign, Donald Trump
couldn’t have made his point more clear:

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.090
he wouldn’t accept any more illegal immigrants.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.090
Right?

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.900
So… check out this chart!

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:35.800
If you pay attention, you will see that, deportations-wise,
Obama was stricter on immigration than Trump.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.300
Does this mean that Trump loves immigrants
and deserves a Peace nobel prize?

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.760
Of course not!

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.660
In fact, there are many nuances to discuss
about this chart.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:48.570
But I wanted to show it to you to make a point:
when it comes to immigration, words are one

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.600
thing and facts are a totally different one.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.470
So why are we talking about this now?

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.650
Because of this…

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:03.270
Migrants at Southern border top 100K for 2nd
month in a row

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:07.280
Yes, you heard that right… at the moment,
the American continent is dealing with one

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.220
of the biggest refugee crises in recent history.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.670
But let’s hear more details about this from
Xander…

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:13.670
But let’s hear more details about this from
Erik…

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:14.670
Of course, Simon!

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:18.299
In recent years, hundreds of thousands of
Central American immigrants have been crossing

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:21.759
Mexican territory until they reach the border
with the US.

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:26.359
Many of them are children and women who make
the whole road by foot and often arrive with

00:01:26.359 --> 00:01:28.579
diseases and malnutrition.

00:01:28.579 --> 00:01:36.860
And yes, I said they cross Mexican soil because
they come from Central America.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:43.939
Countries like Honduras, Guatemala, and El
Salvador have become a living hell: violence,

00:01:43.939 --> 00:01:48.740
drug gangs and, of course, extreme poverty
have caused all of these people to flee their

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:50.869
homelands.

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:55.119
So now you might wonder… how did Trump answer
this challenge?

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:59.119
Of course, he did this…

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:04.060
Donald Trump threatens Mexico with 5% imports
tariff over illegal immigration

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.520
Yes, you heard that right…

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.740
Donald Trump wants to pass the hot potato
to Mexico.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.459
But here is the big question…

00:02:10.459 --> 00:02:12.190
What does Mexico do about it?

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:17.640
First of all, the Mexican President is this
man you see on the screen: ANDRES MANUEL LOPEZ

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.110
OBRADOR, also known as AMLO.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:26.310
AMLO is a hardcore left wing politician who,
you guessed it, is no big fan of Trump.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:30.370
During the electoral campaign, he said he
would be compassionate with immigrants crossing

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:31.380
into his country.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:42.140
But, now he says he’s being pushed by the
White House to take a hard stance on immigration:

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.870
Mexico has a lot to lose if America imposes
tariffs on them.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.970
So AMLO had to send in the troops to stop
the immigrants on the Southern border.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:55.930
So again, evil Donald Trump is pushing a poor,
good hearted politician to do his dirty work,

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:56.930
right?

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:00.860
Well… this is the narrative we have heard
so far on many media outlets.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:03.340
But… is it really that simple?

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.790
For example, here’s a good question… where
would be the big deal if Mexico took in more

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.840
refugees?

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:12.230
Similar arrangements have been made with other
countries like Turkey and they seemed to work…

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.540
but here’s the thing…

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.350
Have you ever wondered about the immigration
policy in Mexico?

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:18.350
Well… you should.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:19.350
Here are some numbers.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.680
14% of the US population are immigrants.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.620
The OCDE average is 13%.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.780
But Mexico has just 1%.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.340
Yes, you heard that right.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.410
Mexico is no country for foreigners.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:34.360
So Today’s question is… how does Mexican
immigration policy actually work?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.310
What is Mexico actually doing to manage the
refugee crisis?

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:39.710
Are they really doing what Trump wants?

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:46.380
Today we are going to answer to all of these
questions but, before we do, let’s take

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:51.040
a look back at the history.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.840
THE MIGRANT CARAVAN

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.930
I know what you’re thinking now… why are
so many central americans leaving their countries

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:58.930
now?

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:03.950
Let’s be honest here, Honduras, Guatemala,
and El Salvador have never been prosperous

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:04.950
countries.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:10.840
But… if we have learned anything from history,
it’s that what goes bad can go even worse.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:16.590
Between 2010 and 2012, the crime rates skyrocketed
here.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.510
Honduras suffered a coup d’etat in 2009.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:23.040
El Salvador is suffering street violence from
the so-called MARAS, or street gangs.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.600
Something similar is happening in Guatemala.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:29.180
And part of it can be explained because of
drug trafficking.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:38.410
You see, during the 80s, narco violence was
focused on Colombia.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:41.990
Those were the times of Pablo Escobar, the
Cali cartel, and the FARC.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.470
But after 2000, Colombia managed to reduce
the violence.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:49.880
Yes, cocaine production is still there, but
the different cartels have reached a sort

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:51.690
of PAX MAFIOSA.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:55.570
They are still in the drug business, but they
don’t kill each other.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:59.540
But now, a similar kind of drug violence has
moved to other parts of the continent.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.800
Also, some people blame climate change.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.470
According to this theory, Climate Change is
creating droughts in Central America.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:09.110
If the crops aren’t productive, people starve
and have to leave.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:15.160
Add to this NGOs like PUEBLOS SIN FRONTERAS,
which organize the so-called migrante caravans.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:19.270
They offer logistical support so thousands
of migrants can start their journeys to the

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:20.270
US border.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:22.150
But of course, it’s not only about NGOs.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:30.620
It’s also about human traffickers.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:37.560
As you can see, there are many explanations,
but the truth is this is an exodus.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:42.870
For a better understanding, in 2007, the US
border patrols apprehended 16,000 Guatemalans.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:47.470
11 years later, in 2018, the figure increased
to 116,000 Guatemalans.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:51.970
And now you might wonder… are these Immigrants
or refugees?

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:56.320
And to be fair, we should talk about refugees.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.830
Officially, they are considered economic migrants
but, let’s be honest… these are not ambitious

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.970
people trying to achieve the American dream.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.230
In most cases, they’re just people escaping
extreme violence.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:11.139
In many cases, they’re women and children
threatened by a Mara or a drug gang.

00:06:11.139 --> 00:06:14.020
They would almost certainly be killed if they
went back.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:17.790
This is why they’ll do whatever it takes
to leave.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:20.770
And I say whatever it takes because they really
take no prisoners.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:27.680
There are more than 3000 kilometers or 1800
miles between Guatemala and El Paso, Texas.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.200
Many of these migrants do the journey by foot.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:38.600
Others do it by the so-called, ‘death train’…
you can imagine why they call it this.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:41.199
So what happens when these people cross the
border?

00:06:41.199 --> 00:06:43.760
Most of them are apprehended and deported
to their home countries.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.880
But let’s be fair here!

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.430
Some make it to America.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:52.070
US authorities have already created many programs
to attend to those refugees.

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:56.210
Just in 2017, more than 59,000 Central Americans
stayed in the country.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:58.500
Is that too much or too little?

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:01.260
It’s up to you to make your own judgment.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:04.870
But the question is… how many did Mexico
accept?

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.820
We don’t have the exact number, but is much
smaller.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.250
Here’s a number we can give you.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:15.510
In Mexico today, there are about 50,000 Guatemalans
while America hosts 900,000.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:20.240
And you might wonder… why?

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.190
Why can’t central americans refugees remain
in Mexico?

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:30.310
Let’s have a look, shall we?

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.229
NO COUNTRY FOR FOREIGNERS

00:07:32.229 --> 00:07:35.900
In Mexico they’ve made it very clear: not
all migrants are made equal.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:40.090
For example, if you are watching this video
from America... don’t worry!

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:42.960
Mexico welcomes you with open arms.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:46.449
In fact, most of the migrants living there
come from the States.

00:07:46.449 --> 00:07:47.580
Don’t believe me?

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:55.419
Look at this chart.

00:07:55.419 --> 00:07:58.240
Mexico has 1,200,000 migrants today.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:06.090
Of those, 900,000 are American, 27,000 are
Spanish, and Only 15,000 come from Honduras.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:08.970
Mexico has more Germans than Salvadoreans.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:13.680
And this is surprising considering that Salvadoreans
are much closer, speak the same language,

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.480
and are leaving their country by the thousands.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:18.480
And you might wonder… why is this?

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:19.880
Is it pure chance?

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.430
Do central Americans don’t like Mexico?

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.440
Of course not.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.590
Just look at what the Mexican immigration
law says.

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:34.810
The Secretary of Government can neglect the
entry to the country to a foreigner or change

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:41.640
the characteristics of their migrant status
anytime the demographic balance requires it

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:46.510
Yes, you heard that right… this demographic
balance is just a nice way of saying; poor

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:48.560
people are not allowed here.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:53.200
And when it says ‘changing the characteristics
of their migrant status’, it basically means

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:55.940
they can kick you out any time they want.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:56.940
But OK!

00:08:56.940 --> 00:08:57.940
OK!

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:58.940
I know what many of you might say.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:08:59.940
Things are changing.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:00.940
And, of course, they are.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:06.650
Just look at what the former Mexican president
said in October 2018.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.880
Today Mexico gives you its hand.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:14.529
We want you and all the migrants to feel protected
and calm.

00:09:14.529 --> 00:09:23.080
In order to support you, Mexico is launching
today the ‘Feel like home!’ plan.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:29.550
Here, in Mexico, you can receive healthcare
assistance, education and you will have a

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:33.890
temporary ID to get your residence permit.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:38.740
The man you see on the screen is ENRIQUE PENA
NIETO, the former Mexican president.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:41.490
This was one of his last policies before leaving
office.

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:44.380
His successor, AMLO agreed with this plan.

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:46.200
And Donald Trump also agreed.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:50.250
All of a sudden, his Southern neighbour accepted
migrants so America didn’t have to.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:54.000
But… wait a minute because, as we said at
the beginning, words are one thing and facts

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.000
are another.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.510
Sure, at the beginning, the Mexican government
accepted people from Central America.

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:03.220
In a few months, more than 20,000 Guatemalans,
Hondurans and Salvadoreans came to the country

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:04.870
asking for a visa.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.041
And how did Mexicans like that?

00:10:06.041 --> 00:10:08.580
Well… not so much!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:18.500
According to a Survey, 58% of Mexicans don’t
want migrants to enter the country.

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:22.180
Exactly! Trump is not alone in hating migrants
and refugees.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:25.170
Add to this the fact that Mexican authorities
can’t deal with so many people crossing

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:26.430
the Southern border.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:31.880
Think about it… you need to build shelters,
print those visas, and feed all those people.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:33.290
And you need money for that.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:34.440
And… political capital.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:37.900
And the new Mexican president doesn’t want
to risk any of those two things.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:41.350
He is extremely popular and he doesn’t want
that to stop being the case.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:46.000
So, with Mexican society against migrants
and the army and the police with no resources,

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:53.760
the new Mexican president had only one choice.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:58.000
Mexico triples deportations of Central Americans
with LOPEZ OBRADOR

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:02.370
The new Government has removed more than 45,000
people in 5 months.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.350
15,000 of those were in April.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:08.490
So now you might wonder… what are the consequences
of this policy?

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:12.720
Of course, the biggest victims are those hundreds
of thousands Central Americans who cannot

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:14.330
stay in Mexico or America.

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:16.470
But this is not the only consequence.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:20.250
Think about it… if AMLO doesn’t want the
refugees… where will they go?

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:21.250
Exactly!

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:25.640
They keep making their way up to the States.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:29.630
So the hot potato falls back into Donald Trump’s
hands.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:35.350
This is in May 2019 and it’s when the White
House threatens Mexico with 5% tariffs.

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:40.780
In other words, this is when the Mexican government
finds itself between the hammer and the anvil.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:45.480
If the Mexican president takes in so many
refugees, Mexicans will hate him.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.740
If he doesn’t… Trump will punish him.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.550
So what’s his solution?

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:54.300
Well… just look…

00:11:54.300 --> 00:12:00.220
U.S. Government's 'Remain in Mexico' Policy
is Expanding, Stranding More People in a Dangerous

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:01.580
Mexican City

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:05.089
In other words, in May 2019, Trump went to
AMLO and said…

00:12:05.089 --> 00:12:06.230
Look, Mexico, dude…

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:10.399
I don’t give two shits about what you do
with Central Americans.

00:12:10.399 --> 00:12:11.399
Really.

00:12:11.399 --> 00:12:12.399
Not my problem…

00:12:12.399 --> 00:12:13.399
Wanna take them?

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:14.399
All yours!

00:12:14.399 --> 00:12:15.399
Wanna deport them?

00:12:15.399 --> 00:12:16.399
Of course!

00:12:16.399 --> 00:12:17.399
You can deport them to…

00:12:17.399 --> 00:12:18.500
Canada, Russia or Mars…

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:24.529
I just don’t wanna see one more of those
people crossing my border!

00:12:24.529 --> 00:12:30.400
And if I do… you’ll pay for it!’

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:32.730
So what was the easiest solution to AMLO?

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:37.100
Basically, letting all those immigrants stay
in a ghetto.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:40.040
Mexico has deployed 6000 troops to contain
them.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:44.100
So they haven’t been deported, but they
cannot continue on their way or integrate

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.260
into Mexican society.

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:49.459
For example, in the most recent months, many
of those immigrants have been concentrated

00:12:49.459 --> 00:12:56.790
in cities like NUEVO LAREDO, at the border
with US, in really poor conditions.

00:12:56.790 --> 00:13:01.880
There are no doctors, no food, and violence
is starting to rise.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:09.600
But the worst place of all is the city of
TAPACHULA, at the border with GUATEMALA.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:13.240
Over 20,000 and 30,000 asylum pledges have
been registered here.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:18.860
And the Mexican army is stationed here, stopping
people from going any farther north.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.950
Lots of murders have been happening already.

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:25.180
So, in other words, those refugees ended up
in the same situation that they were escaping

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:26.180
from.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.250
Neither America nor Mexico wants them.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:36.149
And while they keep passing the hot potato
to each other, people are dying.

00:13:36.149 --> 00:13:38.120
So the question now goes to you…

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:39.630
How do you think this problem could be solved?

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:45.279
Do you think Mexico could do anything to accept
the refugees or is it only America’s job?

00:13:45.279 --> 00:13:48.550
Could they reach a deal to share responsibility?

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:51.279
Please, leave your answer in the comment section
below.

